# Every text file is LF in the repo and in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says. A CRLF
# checkout (Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true) breaks shebang scripts under Vitest
# ("#!/usr/bin/env node\r" is a SyntaxError), tests that match source text with \n regexes, and
# every bash script ($'\r': command not found).
# The 20 files already stored with CRLF or mixed endings keep their bytes: under text=auto, git add,
# status and diff leave a blob that holds CR alone. `git hash-object` does not read the index and still
# cleans them to LF, so the base-tree swap (scripts/gauntlet/swap.sh) also accepts a file whose raw bytes
# are the ref's blob. Do NOT renormalise them (git add --renormalize): they are identical in the older
# refs the swap uses (b230d7ff, 9716aa89), so a swap rewrites one only when the working tree edited it;
# renormalised, every swap would write them back with CRLF over an LF index, and the runner's tree
# check (scripts/gauntlet/lib/stamp.mjs, git diff <ref>) would read them as changed.
# A file with lone CRs (every line CR CR LF: a tool translated LF to CRLF twice) is not text to
# text=auto, so no rule here converts it and git add --renormalize leaves it as it is; an explicit
# `text` would only turn CR CR LF into CRLF and dirty the 20 files above. `git ls-files --eol` shows
# such a file as i/-text: rewrite its bytes to LF (tr -d '\r') and check `git diff -w` is empty.
# The sync-standings route was one (2026-10, PR #65 follow-ups) and is LF now.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The gauntlet capture tools run under Git Bash, and the runner refuses CRLF queue files.
scripts/gauntlet/** text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never convert.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.glb binary
*.hdr binary
*.ktx2 binary
*.wasm binary
*.mp4 binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.xlsx binary
